===============================================================================
                     TuxFrw-NFT Installation Guide
===============================================================================

This document describes the installation, initial configuration, and activation
procedures for TuxFrw-NFT on GNU/Linux systems.

For complete documentation regarding rules and architectural modules, see:
- README (or README.pt-br for Brazilian Portuguese)
- manual/tuxfrw-manual-5.00-en.txt (or manual/tuxfrw-manual-5.00-br.txt)


1. Prerequisites
================

Before installing TuxFrw-NFT, verify that the host meets the following
requirements:

- Operating System: GNU/Linux (Debian, Ubuntu, AlmaLinux, Rocky Linux, RHEL, etc.);
- Linux Kernel: Kernel with Netfilter/nftables support (kernel 4.19 or higher recommended);
- nftables utility: 'nftables' package installed ('nft' command version 0.9.0 or higher);
- Shell: Bash interpreter (/bin/bash);
- Privileges: Superuser (root) access.

To install nftables on Debian/Ubuntu:
# apt update && apt install nftables -y

To install nftables on AlmaLinux/Rocky Linux/RHEL:
# dnf install nftables -y


2. Installation Procedure
=========================

1) Extract sources or clone the repository on the target server:
# git clone https://github.com/gondimcodes/tuxfrw-nft.git
# cd tuxfrw-nft

2) Run the installation script as root:
# ./install.sh

The installer performs the following actions:
- Validates prerequisites (Bash, nftables, etc.);
- Creates configuration directory /etc/tuxfrw-nft (permissions 0700);
- Installs rule modules and configurations with restricted permissions (0600);
- Copies the main CLI executable to /usr/sbin/tuxfrw-nft (permissions 0700);
- Deploys the systemd service unit /etc/systemd/system/tuxfrw-nft.service and
  reloads systemd daemons (systemctl daemon-reload);
- If an existing installation is detected, prompts for explicit confirmation
  before overwriting files.

IMPORTANT: For security and safety reasons, the service is NOT automatically
enabled at boot time during installation. This prevents accidental lockouts
before administrators can review and tailor their rules to the environment.


3. Initial Configuration
=========================

Before starting the firewall for the first time, review and adjust configuration files:

1) Edit /etc/tuxfrw-nft/tuxfrw.conf:
   - Choose the operational mode using the DOCKER_SUPPORT variable:
     * DOCKER_SUPPORT="1" -> Application servers running Docker (preserves bridges
                             and daemon rules, enables tf_DOCKER.mod in FORWARD).
     * DOCKER_SUPPORT="0" -> Classic Gateway / Edge Router mode with NAT.
   - Define your network interfaces (e.g. IF_EXT="eth0", IF_INT="eth1", etc.).
   - Configure administrative IPs and management ports (ADMIN_IPS, ADMIN_PORTS).
   - Review BOGONS parameter (default "0", safe for RFC 1918 corporate networks).

2) Review rule modules under /etc/tuxfrw-nft/rules/:
   - rules/tf_INPUT.mod   -> Host defense rules (SSH, ICMP, DNS, local services).
   - rules/tf_DOCKER.mod  -> (Docker Mode) Container published port filtering and policies.
   - rules/tf_FORWARD.mod -> (Gateway Mode) Routing between INT, EXT, and DMZ networks.
   - rules/tf_NETDEV.mod  -> Ingress-stage pre-filtering on physical interfaces.


4. Runtime Testing (Preventing Lockouts)
========================================

1) Start TuxFrw-NFT manually:
# tuxfrw-nft start

2) Verify the status of loaded tables and chains:
# tuxfrw-nft status

3) Audit live kernel rules directly with nftables:
# nft list ruleset

4) Test external connectivity, Docker containers (if applicable), and SSH access.
   Always keep a backup contingency SSH session active during initial rule trials.


5. Enabling at Boot (Systemd)
=============================

Once rules are tested and verified to operate properly:

# systemctl enable tuxfrw-nft

To manage the service via systemd:
# systemctl start tuxfrw-nft
# systemctl stop tuxfrw-nft
# systemctl restart tuxfrw-nft
# systemctl status tuxfrw-nft


6. Uninstallation
=================

To cleanly remove TuxFrw-NFT from the system:

1) Stop the service and flush TuxFrw tables:
# tuxfrw-nft stop

2) Disable and remove the systemd unit:
# systemctl disable tuxfrw-nft
# rm -f /etc/systemd/system/tuxfrw-nft.service
# systemctl daemon-reload

3) Remove installed files:
# rm -f /usr/sbin/tuxfrw-nft
# rm -rf /etc/tuxfrw-nft
